<Layout title="ATECT Architecture Guide to Choosing Exterior Materials | ATECT Architecture" description="A practical guide to choosing exterior materials by considering durability, maintenance, climate, appearance, and architectural character.">
  <article class="article"><header><p class="eyebrow">Home & Interiors</p><h1>Architect's Guide to Choosing Exterior Materials</h1><p class="lede">Exterior materials influence durability, maintenance, appearance, cost, and the character of a building. The right choice depends on the project—not a single universal material.</p></header>
  <section><h2>Start with performance</h2><p>Consider exposure, moisture, temperature changes, maintenance requirements, expected service life, and how the material will perform at transitions and connections.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Consider the architectural character</h2><p>Materials should support the proportions, massing, openings, roof form, and intended character of the building. A material that works beautifully on one project may not fit another.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Look at the whole assembly</h2><p>Cladding is only one part of an exterior wall or roof assembly. Flashing, drainage, air and water control layers, insulation, trim, and detailing all contribute to performance.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Balance appearance and maintenance</h2><p>Compare the desired look with cleaning, refinishing, replacement, and long-term upkeep before making a final selection.</p></section>
  <section class="callout"><h2>Need help evaluating materials?</h2><p>ATECT Architecture can integrate material decisions into the broader design and documentation process.</p><a class="button dark" href="/contact">Start a Project</a></section>
  </article>
</Layout>
